From: Sanjay Yadav <sanjay.kumar.yadav@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 22:23:18 +0530
Subject: drm/xe/eudebug: Don't queue new attention while debugger has unread events

attention_scan_fn() re-queues an EU_ATTENTION event every 100ms for as
long as threads need attention, regardless of whether the debugger has
drained what is already pending. If the debugger's per-event handling
takes longer than that, the event fifo backlog grows unbounded and
CREATE/DESTROY events queued during workload teardown land behind it,
missing the read window(disconnect + GT reset).

Skip queueing a new attention event while the fifo still has unread
events xe_eudebug_handle_gt_attention() already treats the resulting
-EBUSY as a retry-next-scan, so no reset is triggered.

Cc: Maciej Patelczyk <maciej.patelczyk@intel.com>
Cc: Andrzej Hajda <andrzej.hajda@intel.com>
Reviewed-by: Jan Sokolowski <jan.sokolowski@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Sanjay Yadav <sanjay.kumar.yadav@intel.com>
(backported from commit 8aa56c9b878b306357f193a455df31fe06a1acc5 drm-tip-eudebug)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/prelim/xe_eudebug.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/prelim/xe_eudebug.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/prelim/xe_eudebug.c
index 92aba086ef02..0c52aba0d20d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/prelim/xe_eudebug.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/prelim/xe_eudebug.c
@@ -1742,6 +1742,15 @@ static int xe_send_gt_attention(struct xe_gt *gt)
 		goto err_eudebug_put;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Skip queuing another EU_ATTENTION event while the debugger still
+	 * has unread events in the FIFO. Retry on next scan.
+	 */
+	if (event_fifo_num_events_peek(d)) {
+		ret = -EBUSY;
+		goto err_eudebug_put;
+	}
+
 	ret = send_attention_event(d, q, lrc_idx);
 	if (ret)
 		xe_eudebug_disconnect(d, ret);
